[I] A lightweight, low-memory character encoding detector

[T] detenc is a fast character encoding detector for Western European text.
[T] It determines whether a file is US-ASCII, UTF-8, ISO-8859-15,
[T] WINDOWS-1252 or something else, and can distinguish the latter two where
[T] Euro signs are present.

[U] https://github.com/reevoo/detenc

[A] Detenc Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/base
[F] CROSS

[V] 2.0.0
[L] MIT

